  "status_text": "A hundred clues can boil down to three questions, and the circuit still counts every match. Lean checked this for either switch-ring mixing rule. Give the circuit a base key, requested histories after changes, target lights and parity clues about the round settings. With a cap of three independent parity clues, the exponential factor in its gate bound is at most eight. The size grows only polynomially with the number of clues. Within the cap the count of matching names and schedules is exact. Above it the circuit flags overflow and returns zero (L-meta-25894).",
